  25:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   ==============================================================================
  26:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****                         ##### How to use this driver #####
  27:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   ==============================================================================
  28:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
  29:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     This driver implements a high level communication layer for read and write from/to
  30:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     this memory. The needed STM32 hardware resources (SDIO and GPIO) are performed by
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccPg4sKI.s 			page 2


  31:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     the user in HAL_SD_MspInit() function (MSP layer).
  32:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     Basically, the MSP layer configuration should be the same as we provide in the
  33:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     examples.
  34:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     You can easily tailor this configuration according to hardware resources.
  35:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  36:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
  37:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     This driver is a generic layered driver for SDIO memories which uses the HAL
  38:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     SDIO driver functions to interface with SD and uSD cards devices.
  39:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     It is used as follows:
  40:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  41:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#)Initialize the SDIO low level resources by implementing the HAL_SD_MspInit() API:
  42:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) Enable the SDIO interface clock using __HAL_RCC_SDIO_CLK_ENABLE();
  43:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) SDIO pins configuration for SD card
  44:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Enable the clock for the SDIO GPIOs using the functions __HAL_RCC_GPIOx_CLK_ENABL
  45:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Configure these SDIO pins as alternate function pull-up using HAL_GPIO_Init()
  46:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****                   and according to your pin assignment;
  47:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) DMA configuration if you need to use DMA process (HAL_SD_ReadBlocks_DMA()
  48:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****              and HAL_SD_WriteBlocks_DMA() APIs).
  49:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Enable the DMAx interface clock using __HAL_RCC_DMAx_CLK_ENABLE();
  50:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Configure the DMA using the function HAL_DMA_Init() with predeclared and filled.
  51:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) NVIC configuration if you need to use interrupt process when using DMA transfer.
  52:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Configure the SDIO and DMA interrupt priorities using functions
  53:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****                   HAL_NVIC_SetPriority(); DMA priority is superior to SDIO's priority
  54:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Enable the NVIC DMA and SDIO IRQs using function HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ()
  55:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) SDIO interrupts are managed using the macros __HAL_SD_ENABLE_IT()
  56:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****                   and __HAL_SD_DISABLE_IT() inside the communication process.
  57:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) SDIO interrupts pending bits are managed using the macros __HAL_SD_GET_IT()
  58:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****                   and __HAL_SD_CLEAR_IT()
  59:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) NVIC configuration if you need to use interrupt process (HAL_SD_ReadBlocks_IT()
  60:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****              and HAL_SD_WriteBlocks_IT() APIs).
  61:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Configure the SDIO interrupt priorities using function HAL_NVIC_SetPriority();
  62:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Enable the NVIC SDIO IRQs using function HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ()
  63:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) SDIO interrupts are managed using the macros __HAL_SD_ENABLE_IT()
  64:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****                   and __HAL_SD_DISABLE_IT() inside the communication process.
  65:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) SDIO interrupts pending bits are managed using the macros __HAL_SD_GET_IT()
  66:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****                   and __HAL_SD_CLEAR_IT()
  67:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) At this stage, you can perform SD read/write/erase operations after SD card initialization
  68:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  69:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  70:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   *** SD Card Initialization and configuration ***
  71:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   ================================================
  72:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
  73:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     To initialize the SD Card, use the HAL_SD_Init() function. It Initializes
  74:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     SDIO Peripheral(STM32 side) and the SD Card, and put it into StandBy State (Ready for data tran
  75:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     This function provide the following operations:
  76:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  77:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) Apply the SD Card initialization process at 400KHz and check the SD Card
  78:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         type (Standard Capacity or High Capacity). You can change or adapt this
  79:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         frequency by adjusting the "ClockDiv" field.
  80:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         The SD Card frequency (SDIO_CK) is computed as follows:
  81:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  82:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****            SDIO_CK = SDIOCLK / (ClockDiv + 2)
  83:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  84:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         In initialization mode and according to the SD Card standard,
  85:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         make sure that the SDIO_CK frequency doesn't exceed 400KHz.
  86:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  87:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         This phase of initialization is done through SDIO_Init() and
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccPg4sKI.s 			page 3


  88:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         SDIO_PowerState_ON() SDIO low level APIs.
  89:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  90:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) Initialize the SD card. The API used is HAL_SD_InitCard().
  91:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         This phase allows the card initialization and identification
  92:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         and check the SD Card type (Standard Capacity or High Capacity)
  93:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         The initialization flow is compatible with SD standard.
  94:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  95:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         This API (HAL_SD_InitCard()) could be used also to reinitialize the card in case
  96:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         of plug-off plug-in.
  97:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  98:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) Configure the SD Card Data transfer frequency. You can change or adapt this
  99:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         frequency by adjusting the "ClockDiv" field.
 100:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         In transfer mode and according to the SD Card standard, make sure that the
 101:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         SDIO_CK frequency doesn't exceed 25MHz and 50MHz in High-speed mode switch.
 102:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         To be able to use a frequency higher than 24MHz, you should use the SDIO
 103:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         peripheral in bypass mode. Refer to the corresponding reference manual
 104:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         for more details.
 105:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 106:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) Select the corresponding SD Card according to the address read with the step 2.
 107:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 108:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) Configure the SD Card in wide bus mode: 4-bits data.
 109:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 110:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   *** SD Card Read operation ***
 111:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   ==============================
 112:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
 113:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (+) You can read from SD card in polling mode by using function HAL_SD_ReadBlocks().
 114:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 115:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
 116:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 117:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 118:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 119:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         through HAL_SD_GetCardState() function for SD card state.
 120:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 121:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (+) You can read from SD card in DMA mode by using function HAL_SD_ReadBlocks_DMA().
 122:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 123:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
 124:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 125:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 126:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 127:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         through HAL_SD_GetCardState() function for SD card state.
 128:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         You could also check the DMA transfer process through the SD Rx interrupt event.
 129:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 130:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (+) You can read from SD card in Interrupt mode by using function HAL_SD_ReadBlocks_IT().
 131:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 132:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
 133:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 134:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 135:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 136:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         through HAL_SD_GetCardState() function for SD card state.
 137:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         You could also check the IT transfer process through the SD Rx interrupt event.
 138:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
